{
 "lang": "en",
 "duration": 110.6909375,
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.04,
   "text": "The biggest mistake people make after a painful experience"
  },
  {
   "start": 3.04,
   "end": 5.74,
   "text": "is trying to get past it as quickly as possible."
  },
  {
   "start": 6.04,
   "end": 8.24,
   "text": "Move on, stay busy, don't think about it."
  },
  {
   "start": 8.26,
   "end": 10.26,
   "text": "That sounds healthy, but it isn't."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.44,
   "end": 13.64,
   "text": "I spent years treating suffering as a problem to solve,"
  },
  {
   "start": 13.96,
   "end": 15.84,
   "text": "to get through it, to put it behind me,"
  },
  {
   "start": 15.96,
   "end": 17.2,
   "text": "to get back to normal,"
  },
  {
   "start": 17.3,
   "end": 20.3,
   "text": "and I kept noticing in my own life and in the research"
  },
  {
   "start": 20.3,
   "end": 23.98,
   "text": "that the people who did that actually didn't heal faster."
  },
  {
   "start": 24.1,
   "end": 27.0,
   "text": "They just stopped feeling, which is not the same thing."
  },
  {
   "start": 27.0,
   "end": 30.48,
   "text": "We're wired to avoid pain because pain signals danger."
  },
  {
   "start": 30.64,
   "end": 32.18,
   "text": "That was useful for survival."
  },
  {
   "start": 32.44,
   "end": 35.32,
   "text": "It's much less useful for building a meaningful life"
  },
  {
   "start": 35.32,
   "end": 37.16,
   "text": "because some of the most important things"
  },
  {
   "start": 37.16,
   "end": 39.56,
   "text": "that will ever happen to you will hurt,"
  },
  {
   "start": 39.56,
   "end": 41.24,
   "text": "and if you rush past the lesson,"
  },
  {
   "start": 41.48,
   "end": 43.76,
   "text": "you lose what it was trying to show you."
  },
  {
   "start": 43.94,
   "end": 45.28,
   "text": "The Buddhists have understood this"
  },
  {
   "start": 45.28,
   "end": 47.14,
   "text": "for two and a half thousand years."
  },
  {
   "start": 47.44,
   "end": 49.14,
   "text": "Modern psychology is catching up."
  },
  {
   "start": 49.28,
   "end": 51.34,
   "text": "Researchers who study post-traumatic growth"
  },
  {
   "start": 51.34,
   "end": 53.12,
   "text": "keep finding the same pattern."
  },
  {
   "start": 53.22,
   "end": 54.98,
   "text": "People who sit with their suffering,"
  },
  {
   "start": 54.98,
   "end": 59.08,
   "text": "who ask what is teaching them rather than how to escape it,"
  },
  {
   "start": 59.1,
   "end": 60.54,
   "text": "often come out with something"
  },
  {
   "start": 60.54,
   "end": 62.54,
   "text": "the comfortable life never gave them."
  },
  {
   "start": 62.82,
   "end": 65.12,
   "text": "Sharper priorities, deeper relationships,"
  },
  {
   "start": 65.42,
   "end": 67.7,
   "text": "a clearer sense of what actually matters."
  },
  {
   "start": 67.94,
   "end": 70.02,
   "text": "The practice I give my students is simple."
  },
  {
   "start": 70.26,
   "end": 71.56,
   "text": "When something painful happens,"
  },
  {
   "start": 71.82,
   "end": 73.54,
   "text": "don't ask, how do I get over this?"
  },
  {
   "start": 73.92,
   "end": 76.58,
   "text": "Ask instead, what is this trying to teach me?"
  },
  {
   "start": 76.7,
   "end": 79.34,
   "text": "That's a different project, and it's a harder one,"
  },
  {
   "start": 79.42,
   "end": 81.08,
   "text": "but it's the one that leads somewhere."
  },
  {
   "start": 81.22,
   "end": 83.62,
   "text": "That question, what is this trying to show me,"
  },
  {
   "start": 83.62,
   "end": 86.02,
   "text": "is what the meaning membership is built around."
  },
  {
   "start": 86.36,
   "end": 88.84,
   "text": "Every month, we take one of life's biggest questions"
  },
  {
   "start": 88.84,
   "end": 91.1,
   "text": "and examine it together, through research,"
  },
  {
   "start": 91.46,
   "end": 94.28,
   "text": "through ancient wisdom, and through honest conversation."
  },
  {
   "start": 94.56,
   "end": 96.24,
   "text": "Not to arrive at easy answers,"
  },
  {
   "start": 96.46,
   "end": 97.82,
   "text": "but to become the kind of people"
  },
  {
   "start": 97.82,
   "end": 99.7,
   "text": "who can hold the real answers."
  },
  {
   "start": 100.02,
   "end": 102.02,
   "text": "Because meaning isn't something you find once,"
  },
  {
   "start": 102.34,
   "end": 103.78,
   "text": "it's something that accumulates,"
  },
  {
   "start": 104.16,
   "end": 106.68,
   "text": "and it accumulates fastest when you stop running"
  },
  {
   "start": 106.68,
   "end": 109.24,
   "text": "from the things that are trying to teach you."
  }
 ],
